tion.\n2. Emit the immutable result record named by ADR 0001.\n3. Include review identity, final disposition, and covered evidence IDs.\n4. Summarize the result record to the operator.\n# Review domain language\n\nProtocol terms are authoritative in [`docs/protocol-glossary.md`](docs/protocol-glossary.md). This glossary defines only concepts introduced by the review layer and does not restate upstream terms.\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Review | A bounded adjudication of evidence against one target. |\n| Result record | The review layer's current name for the terminal artifact emitted when a review closes. |\n# Protocol glossary\n\n**Receipt:** An immutable terminal record of one completed state transition, including its outcome and stable identity.\n\n**External owner:** The authority outside the reviewed package that positively owns a concluded defect.\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).\n","exit_code":128,"status":"failed"}}
